    "<a id=\"introduction\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. 📖 Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This section introduces the business context of customer churn, the problem being solved, and the dataset used throughout the project.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "950210c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1.1 Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer churn is one of the biggest challenges faced by subscription-based businesses such as telecom companies, banks, insurance providers, and online streaming platforms. Losing existing customers can significantly impact a company's revenue and growth.\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this project is to develop a Machine Learning model that predicts whether a customer is likely to leave the company's service based on their demographic information, account details, and service usage patterns.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project covers the complete Machine Learning pipeline, including data understanding, data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), feature engineering, data preprocessing, model building, model evaluation, and model comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "By identifying customers who are at risk of churning, businesses can take proactive actions to improve customer retention and reduce revenue loss.\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer churn prediction is a binary classification problem that aims to identify customers who are likely to leave a company. In this project, exploratory data analysis (EDA), data cleaning, feature engineering, and multiple machine learning models were applied to predict customer churn. The models were evaluated using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-Score, and ROC-AUC Score to identify the best-performing algorithm.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ccc31488",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.2 Business Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer retention is more cost-effective than acquiring new customers. However, businesses often struggle to identify customers who are likely to discontinue their services.\n",
    "\n",
    "The challenge is to accurately predict customer churn using historical customer data. A reliable prediction model enables businesses to take preventive measures, such as offering personalized discounts, improving customer support, or providing loyalty benefits to retain valuable customers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76278642",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.3 Dataset Information\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset used in this project is the **Telco Customer Churn** dataset, downloaded from **Kaggle**.\n",
    "\n",
    "It contains customer demographic information, account details, subscribed services, billing information, and the customer's churn status.\n",
