   "source": [
    "### Observation\n",
    "\n",
    "The `isnull()` function reported **zero missing values** in the dataset. However, after further investigation, the `TotalCharges` column was found to contain **11 blank spaces** (`\" \"`).\n",
    "\n",
    "These blank spaces are not recognized as missing values by Pandas because they are stored as strings instead of `NaN`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fb094664",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.2 Handling Hidden Missing Values\n",
    "\n",
    "The blank spaces in the `TotalCharges` column are replaced with `NaN` so that Pandas can recognize them as missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "After replacing the blank values, the column is converted from the `object` data type to a numeric data type."
   ]
