   "id": "5418b2cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5.13 EDA Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The exploratory data analysis identified several factors that influence customer churn.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key findings include:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Gender has little impact on customer churn.\n",
    "- Senior citizens are more likely to churn than non-senior customers.\n",
    "- Customers without partners or dependents have higher churn rates.\n",
    "- Fiber optic internet users experience the highest churn among internet service types.\n",
    "- Customers without online security or technical support are more likely to leave the company.\n",
    "- Month-to-month contracts have the highest churn rate, while two-year contracts have the lowest.\n",
    "- Customers using electronic checks are more likely to churn than those using automatic payment methods.\n",
    "- Customers with higher monthly charges tend to churn more frequently.\n",
    "- Customers with shorter tenure are significantly more likely to churn than long-term customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, contract type, tenure, internet service, online security, technical support, and monthly charges appear to be the strongest factors associated with customer churn."
   ]
