    "XGBoost achieved **79.46% accuracy** and a **ROC-AUC of 0.838**, with churn-class precision of **63%** and recall of **55%**. This is essentially on par with the tuned Random Forest and marginally ahead of Logistic Regression on ROC-AUC (0.838 vs 0.836), though Logistic Regression still edges it out on churn recall (57% vs 55%).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Insight\n",
    "\n",
    "With default-ish settings, XGBoost does not dramatically outperform a well-tuned Random Forest or a simple Logistic Regression on this dataset — this is common on datasets of this size (~7,000 rows) with mostly categorical, linearly-separable signals. Its main value here would come from further tuning (learning rate, tree depth, regularization) or from its native handling of missing values in a production pipeline, rather than from a large out-of-the-box accuracy gain."
