    "\n",
    "# 14. 🎚️ Threshold Tuning & Precision-Recall Trade-off\n",
    "\n",
    "By default, a customer is classified as \"Churn\" only if the predicted probability is above 0.5. In a churn-prevention business context, missing an actual churner (a false negative) is often more costly than flagging a loyal customer for a retention offer (a false positive). Lowering the decision threshold trades some precision for higher recall — catching more true churners at the cost of more false alarms."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 104,
   "id": "b59a749f",
   "metadata": {
